# Build output and local state never belong in the build context: they bloat every layer, and a bin/
# from the host can silently shadow what the build stage just produced.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
artifacts/
TestResults/

# Visual Studio per-developer files. These carry local launch profiles and, occasionally, connection
# strings — they must reach neither the context nor an image layer.
**/*.user
**/*.suo
.vs/
.idea/

# WSL writes an alternate data stream beside files copied from Windows. Harmless on disk, noise in
# the context — and they will otherwise be COPYd into the image.
**/*:Zone.Identifier

# Secrets and local storage
.env
ged-storage/
**/appsettings.*.local.json

# Not read by any build
.git/
.github/
*.md
docs/
LICENSE
compose*.yaml
docker-compose*.yml
docker-compose.dcproj
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.editorconfig

# NOTE: libraries/ is deliberately NOT ignored. MicroKit is vendored as source, and a restore that
# cannot see it fails on the first ProjectReference.
